summary:
MyFin Budget is a personal finance web app (React SPA with an Express API), signed in as the seeded user 'marta'. I saved 5 views, and each one reached the same screen when replayed: 
1) dashboard: monthly overview gauge, monthly savings bars, and income and expense donut charts, under the net-worth summary chips; 
2) transactions: the transactions table with account flow, category and entity, value, and edit/delete actions; 
3) budget-detail (/#/budget/23): the November 2026 budget editor with summary cards and debit/credit category cards; 
4) investments-summary (/#/invest/dashboard): asset-class donut chart, top performers list and return stat cards; 
5) stats-net-worth (/#/stats/patrimony): tabbed stats page with an account filter, a net-worth line chart and a monthly table. 

One view was rejected. I tried to save the Edit transaction dialog, but the harness turned it down as a near-duplicate of the transactions view (same URL, similar text), so it isn't included. 

Two quirks: 
- The live session stopped working after each save, apparently because each replay signs in again. I had to sign in again by hand before recording each next view. 
- A "Something went wrong" toast often appeared right after signing in. It went away on its own. The stats view still shows a chart tooltip because the cursor was resting on the chart. 

I didn't capture Accounts, Goals, Categories/Entities/Tags, Rules or Profile.
